<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    title: "Introducing orbitant-os: The Future Will Be AI or Nothing at All",
    description: "We're excited to announce orbitant-os — Orbitant's open-source plugin marketplace for AI agents.",
    template: 'doc',
  }}
>
  <p class="meta">
    <time datetime="2026-03-03">March 3, 2026</time> · Orbitant Team
  </p>

  <p>We're excited to announce <strong>orbitant-os</strong> — Orbitant's open-source plugin marketplace for AI agents.</p>

  <h2 id="why-we-built-this">Why We Built This</h2>

  <p>AI assistants are powerful, but they're also <em>generic</em>. Every time you start a conversation, you're back to square one — explaining context, setting expectations, defining workflows.</p>

  <p>We got tired of it.</p>

  <p>At Orbitant, we use AI agents every day for marketing, operations, communications, and more. We found ourselves writing the same prompts, establishing the same guidelines, and correcting the same mistakes — over and over.</p>

  <p>So we built orbitant-os: a collection of reusable skills, agents, and commands that encode our best practices and make AI actually useful for real work.</p>

  <h2 id="what-makes-it-different">What Makes It Different</h2>

  <p><strong>Skills that activate automatically.</strong> You don't need to remember to invoke them. Writing a blog post? The AI knows to check SEO, readability, and brand tone — because the skill's description tells it when to activate.</p>

  <p><strong>Commands for one-shot actions.</strong> <code>/preflight</code> your day in 30 seconds. <code>/triage</code> your inbox. <code>/prep</code> for a meeting. No lengthy conversations, just results.</p>

  <p><strong>Specialized agents.</strong> Instead of one AI trying to do everything, we have focused sub-agents with restricted tools. The triage agent only reads and categorizes. The enrichment agent only looks up contact info. Constraints make them reliable.</p>

  <h2 id="open-source-open-standard">Open Source, Open Standard</h2>

  <p>orbitant-os is fully open source under MIT license. Fork it, modify it, contribute back.</p>

  <p>We also support the <a href="https://agentskills.io">Agent Skills</a> open standard via <a href="https://skills.sh">skills.sh</a>, which means our skills work with 40+ AI agents — not just Claude.</p>

  <h2 id="whats-available-today">What's Available Today</h2>

  <p><strong>orbitant-marketing</strong> — Blog post review, creation, translation, and brand tone skills for content teams.</p>

  <p><strong>orbitant-chief-of-staff</strong> — An AI executive assistant with 7 commands, 3 skills, and 2 specialized agents for managing priorities, communications, and goal alignment.</p>

  <p>More verticals coming soon: engineering, HR, infrastructure, and beyond.</p>

  <h2 id="get-started">Get Started</h2>

  <pre><code>/plugin marketplace add weorbitant/orbitant-os
/plugin install orbitant-marketing</code></pre>

  <p>That's it. Check out the <a href="/orbitant-os/getting-started/quick-start/">Overview</a> to learn more.</p>

  <h2 id="join-us">Join Us</h2>

  <p>We're building tools for a future where AI handles the grunt work and humans focus on what matters. If that resonates with you:</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Use it</strong> — Install the plugins, give us feedback</li>
    <li><strong>Contribute</strong> — Add your own skills to the marketplace</li>
    <li><strong>Star us</strong> — <a href="https://github.com/weorbitant/orbitant-os">github.com/weorbitant/orbitant-os</a></li>
  </ul>

  <p>The future will be AI or nothing at all. Let's build it together.</p>

  <p><em>— The Orbitant Team</em></p>

